    {
      "id": "text-35",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 912.0,
      "y": 130,
      "width": 236.0,
      "height": 275.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every change this loop\nproposes -- a retrained\nmodel, a new desk weight --\ngoes through the SAME\nPBO / Deflated Sharpe\nvalidation gate as any\nbrand-new strategy\n(page 07).\n\nThe learning loop does not\nget to bypass validation\njust because it's the\nplatform 'learning about\nitself' -- that is exactly\nthe scenario overfitting\nchecks exist for.\n\nSee pbo-deflated-sharpe\nand trading-loop /\nautoresearch skills.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every change this loop\nproposes -- a retrained\nmodel, a new desk weight --\ngoes through the SAME\nPBO / Deflated Sharpe\nvalidation gate as any\nbrand-new strategy\n(page 07).\n\nThe learning loop does not\nget to bypass validation\njust because it's the\nplatform 'learning about\nitself' -- that is exactly\nthe scenario overfitting\nchecks exist for.\n\nSee pbo-deflated-sharpe\nand trading-loop /\nautoresearch skills.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
